	<p>
	Eli Bernard Cowie (they/them) is a professional stagehand, technician, and writer in the Boston Area. Cowie graduated from Wheaton College MA cum laude in 2026 with majors in Theatre and in Economics. As a stagehand and carpenter, they recently worked on CSC's production of Romeo and Juliet on the Boston Common, and at MGM Music Hall at Fenway Park. As a theatremaker and arts manager, they were one of three fellows for the National Theatre Institute Fall semester. As a designer and technical director, they hold the Lillian Hellman Prize for Excellence in Theatre from Wheaton College for their role as Technical Director producing Everybody by Brendan Jacobs-Jenkins and Amadeus by Peter Shaffer. 
	</p>
	<p>
They also attended NTI in the performance track of Fall ‘24. Follow their work at creativeelicowie.com or on instagram at eli.b.cowie.
	</p>
